er have with him and it  just rubs off on  everybody on the set and so it really  was a moment of like  just remembering why this is this is  what i've chosen to do with my life and  that i i do love it  i'm jumping ahead a little here but i  can't not ask about this more  when you did once especially given the  fact that your character  you know she has so much confidence and  exudes so much authority and then you're  working alongside someone you've dreamed  of working with so many other iconic  actors does  does it like click into place for you  immediately or do the nerves still  bubble up in moments like that well you  know it was  again it was very luxurious to be able  to film that sequence  in order you know so the first thing  that i filmed was  literally the shot of me appearing  behind the screen door and like the sun  kind of rising over my face and illumina  and that was  kind of my first thing so that was good  because it's like i didn't have to say  any lines yet you know it was kind of  like more of a physicality thing the  camera was kind of far away i was like  okay  we're easing our way into the like  you know this close-up shot of my  eyebrows okay good we're like  easing me into it a little bit it was  interesting though because i did  feel like the red hair and the brown  contact lenses and the sort of  um freckle makeup and the  the dirt and everything was almost like  a shield like i didn't feel like myself  i  really did feel like another character  and she is such a wild eyed kind of  could do or say anything character that  i i felt  i felt empowered by that um  i was definitely nervous but i but but  again  even though it is a larger-than-life  experience quentin really makes it very  special and very intimate you know he's  like  right there behind the camera and he's  worked with so many of the same people  over and over again which i also think  is something that i've noticed that  a lot of the greats most of the greats  do they keep  